1
00:00:01,610 --> 00:00:08,000
الحمد لله رب العالمين
و الصلاة و السلام على سيّد الأنبياء و المرسلين
و على آله و صحبه أجمعين

2
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:10,180
السلام عليك و رحمة الله و بركاته

3
00:00:10,250 --> 00:00:15,160
We're going to try to understand
a structural analysis of Sūrat al-Qāf rather.

4
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:17,390
The 50th sūra of the Qur'ān.

5
00:00:18,210 --> 00:00:20,610
This sūra is going to be an opportunity for me to

6
00:00:20,610 --> 00:00:24,700
share with you also how some of the symmetrical composition works.

7
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:27,260
Some of the more complex, symmetrical composition works.

8
00:00:27,270 --> 00:00:30,630
It's not like the three āyāt in the beginning

9
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:33,070
are paralleled with the three āyāt at the end.

10
00:00:33,070 --> 00:00:35,360
It's not like that. Don't think of it in terms of number.

11
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:38,050
Don't think of it in terms of wording.

12
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:40,300
It's going to be in terms of subject matter.

13
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:45,360
The parallels that happen or the mirrors that happen are in terms of subject matter.

14
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:47,040
If you remember my discussion on Sūrat al-Nūr

15
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:51,150
you saw that the beginning was mirrored by the end. Social versus political.

16
00:00:52,140 --> 00:00:56,460
But then there was the sabotage effort, followed by council.

17
00:00:57,240 --> 00:01:00,430
If you were mirroring that, you would find council followed,

18
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:01,790
followed by sabotage effort.

19
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:04,860
But you found a parallel sabotage effort, followed by counsel.

20
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:09,280
So it had A - B on one end, and then again A - B on the other end.

21
00:01:09,290 --> 00:01:12,750
Not A - B on this end and then B - A on the other end, you understand?

22
00:01:13,340 --> 00:01:16,540
And similarly, what came in were three sets of permissions

23
00:01:16,540 --> 00:01:18,950
or three sets of regulations A, B and C.

24
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:23,770
And then on the flip side was also instead of being C, B, and A, was still again A, B, and C.

25
00:01:23,780 --> 00:01:25,217
So those are parallels.

26
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:29,140
Sometimes you find in the Qur'ān that they are mirrors.

27
00:01:29,150 --> 00:01:32,310
So it's what was in one order is reversed in the other order,

28
00:01:32,320 --> 00:01:34,930
and sometimes you find them in parallel order.

29
00:01:34,940 --> 00:01:35,450
Okay?

30
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:36,795
So, Sūrat Qāf,

31
00:01:36,820 --> 00:01:40,240
let's begin one section at a time. Before we discuss its overall architecture.

32
00:01:40,250 --> 00:01:43,970
I've color coded them, so it's become a little bit easier for you to visualize.

33
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:45,100
I'll be reading the Arabic,

34
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:48,460
but I'll translate it for you so you can you can know what the message is about.

35
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:50,518
ق وَالْقُرْآنِ الْمَجِيدِ

36
00:01:50,555 --> 00:01:53,888
بَلْ عَجِبُوا أَنْ جَاءَهُمْ مُنْذِرٌ مِنْهُمْ فَقَالَ الْكَافِرُونَ هَذَا شَيْءٌ عَجِيبٌ

37
00:01:53,910 --> 00:01:57,244
أَئِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا ذَلِكَ رَجْعٌ بَعِيدٌ

38
00:01:57,284 --> 00:02:01,028
قَدْ عَلِمْنَا مَا تَنْقُصُ الأَرْضُ مِنْهُمْ وَعِنْدَنَا كِتَابٌ حَفِيظٌ

39
00:02:01,030 --> 00:02:04,185
بَلْ كَذَّبُوا بِالْحَقِّ لَمَّا جَاءَهُمْ فَهُمْ فِي أَمْرٍ مَرِيجٍ

40
00:02:04,370 --> 00:02:09,139
There are a few elements in this passage. One: Allāh is making-- drawing

41
00:02:09,150 --> 00:02:11,850
as evidence the Nobility and the Majesty of the Qur'ān.

42
00:02:12,740 --> 00:02:16,200
He's then saying that the disbelievers have two things to say.

43
00:02:16,210 --> 00:02:19,980
The number one, the first thing they have to say is they find it very strange.

44
00:02:19,990 --> 00:02:22,160
They find this entire message very strange.

45
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:25,335
And then they add to what that strangeness is.

46
00:02:25,390 --> 00:02:27,635
'Well, after we die and we're decayed

47
00:02:27,640 --> 00:02:29,550
how are we going to be brought back into a new life?'

48
00:02:30,340 --> 00:02:33,960
'That seems very far fetched:
رَجْعٌ بَعِيْد.' Okay.

49
00:02:34,340 --> 00:02:37,640
And then Allāh responds by saying: you might think it's far fetched,

50
00:02:37,640 --> 00:02:40,059
but the earth is already taking away from you little by little.

51
00:02:40,809 --> 00:02:43,478
Meaning, your skin cells are
dying every day, and a little of

52
00:02:43,502 --> 00:02:46,170
you-- and every single day the
earth is pulling you into itself.

53
00:02:46,180 --> 00:02:47,200
And even after you die,

54
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:49,050
the earth will start decaying you. And Allāh knows

55
00:02:49,050 --> 00:02:50,860
exactly what that decay is going to be.

56
00:02:51,340 --> 00:02:53,670
But it's the slow process of

57
00:02:53,770 --> 00:02:56,172
death that we are already a part of.

58
00:02:56,540 --> 00:02:58,050
That Allāh, 'azza wa jalla, makes reference to.

59
00:02:58,050 --> 00:03:00,410
قَدْ عَلِمْنَا مَا تَنْقُصُ الأَرْضُ مِنْهُمْ

60
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:03,650
And even though that is decaying, and everything is getting lost,

61
00:03:03,650 --> 00:03:05,660
you're being lost into the earth.

62
00:03:05,630 --> 00:03:07,306
Allāh says:
وَ عِنْدَنَا كِتَابٌ حَفِيظٌ

63
00:03:07,390 --> 00:03:09,960
We have a book that guards all of this.

64
00:03:10,140 --> 00:03:13,160
Physically, you may be lost; but it's still preserved in a book.

65
00:03:13,540 --> 00:03:17,210
And the truth is that they're just confused, and they're lying against this message.

66
00:03:17,220 --> 00:03:20,362
They're calling it a lie because of their doubts.

67
00:03:20,402 --> 00:03:25,050
Now, by the end of this sūra, Allāh says: be patient over what they say.

68
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:28,867
And later on, He says:
نَحْنُ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا يَقُولُونَ

69
00:03:28,860 --> 00:03:30,594
We know what they say.

70
00:03:30,594 --> 00:03:33,094
So "saying" is mentioned twice,

71
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:35,600
Just like what they said. There were two things that they said:

72
00:03:35,610 --> 00:03:37,334
They said "this is a strange thing"

73
00:03:37,374 --> 00:03:40,870
and they said: "We're going to die, how are we going to be brought back?"

74
00:03:40,890 --> 00:03:44,310
And Allāh refers to their saying twice and basically tells the Prophet ﷺ

75
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:46,460
you need to be patient with whatever they're saying,

76
00:03:46,470 --> 00:03:49,260
and you will find patience in whatever they're saying

77
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:51,990
by recognizing that I know what they're saying.

78
00:03:52,490 --> 00:03:55,030
نَحْنُ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا يَقُولُونَ وَمَا أَنْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِجَبَّارٍ

79
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:58,910
Interestingly, also, that passage began with the Nobility,

80
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:00,100
the Majesty of the Qur'ān.

81
00:04:00,090 --> 00:04:01,540
ق وَالْقُرْآنِ الْمَجِيدِ

82
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:07,236
And you find the Qur'ān at the end passage again:
فَذَكِّرْ بِالْقُرْآنِ مَنْ يَخَافُ وَعِيدِ

83
00:04:07,296 --> 00:04:10,260
Remind with the Qur'ān whoever fears the Promise, the Threat.

84
00:04:11,302 --> 00:04:15,050
Interestingly also, the Majesty of the Qur'ān means you don't

85
00:04:15,050 --> 00:04:17,670
have to force anyone to acknowledge how powerful,

86
00:04:17,670 --> 00:04:19,260
how beautiful, how majestic it is.

87
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:22,180
You don't take someone to the most beautiful

88
00:04:22,180 --> 00:04:24,350
architecture or the most incredible scene and say,

89
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:25,550
'Hey, come on, isn't it beautiful?'

90
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:27,280
'Tell me it's beautiful! Please tell me it's beautiful!'

91
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:29,650
It speaks for itself.

92
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:32,050
If you can't see it, that's your problem.

93
00:04:32,940 --> 00:04:34,460
That's not anybody else's problem.

94
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:35,550
Okay?

95
00:04:36,010 --> 00:04:38,264
So, Allāh says:
وَمَا أَنْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِجَبَّارٍ

96
00:04:38,254 --> 00:04:39,550
You're not there to force them.

97
00:04:39,940 --> 00:04:42,050
You're not there to force their hand to acknowledge

98
00:04:42,050 --> 00:04:43,820
the Majesty of the Qur'ān, because it's majestic.

99
00:04:43,820 --> 00:04:47,400
So it's actually furthering the notion of the Majesty of the Qur'ān.

100
00:04:47,410 --> 00:04:49,150
You notice that they said,

101
00:04:50,490 --> 00:04:51,860
ذَلِكَ رَجْعٌ بَعِيدٌ

102
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:54,550
This is a far fetched return.

103
00:04:54,940 --> 00:04:56,520
And Allāh says, in response:

104
00:04:56,529 --> 00:05:00,190
وَاسْتَمِعْ يَوْمَ يُنَادِ الْمُنَادِي مِنْ مَكَانٍ قَرِيبٍ

105
00:05:01,300 --> 00:05:06,050
They see it as far-fetched. Allāh says:
Listen for the day when the caller will call and he is really nearby.

106
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:11,060
So ba'id (بعيد) is contrasted with--far is contrasted with near.

107
00:05:11,730 --> 00:05:15,930
Similarly there Allāh, 'azza wa jalla, described that slowly the earth is taking them away.

108
00:05:16,100 --> 00:05:16,810
You recall?

109
00:05:17,440 --> 00:05:22,170
And here Allāh will say:
يَوْمَ تَشَقَّقُ الأَرْضُ عَنْهُمْ سِرَاعًا

110
00:05:22,640 --> 00:05:24,050
What is (سُرْعَة)?

111
00:05:25,270 --> 00:05:26,960
The earth will spit them out real fast.

112
00:05:27,840 --> 00:05:29,300
It's slowly decaying them,

113
00:05:29,310 --> 00:05:32,160
but on that day, it will tear open and pull them out really quickly.

114
00:05:32,640 --> 00:05:34,500
They were questioning Resurrection,

115
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:38,100
And Allāh  says I don't need to explain My power to resurrect to them.

116
00:05:38,060 --> 00:05:40,560
إِنَّا نَحْنُ نُحْيِي وَنُمِيتُ

117
00:05:40,550 --> 00:05:42,970
We're the ones who give life and give death.

118
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:44,460
And basically the Prophet ﷺ says is told

119
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:46,930
in response to all of their criticisms,

120
00:05:46,930 --> 00:05:51,620
all you need to do is:
وَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ قَبْلَ طُلُوعِ الشَّمْسِ وَقَبْلَ الْغُرُوبِ

121
00:05:51,630 --> 00:05:54,140
You just continue to declare Allāh's perfection.

122
00:05:53,950 --> 00:05:56,850
You see how the opening of the sūra is completed

123
00:05:57,240 --> 00:06:00,030
is responded to by the end of this sūra, right?

124
00:06:00,210 --> 00:06:02,250
Let's go to the second discussion in this sūra.

125
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:05,340
Allāh switches the subject to, okay, fine

126
00:06:05,340 --> 00:06:07,210
you're skeptical about Resurrection,

127
00:06:07,220 --> 00:06:11,400
but have you looked at the world around you with the eyes of faith?

128
00:06:11,474 --> 00:06:16,800
أَفَلَمْ يَنْظُرُوا إِلَى السَّمَاءِ فَوْقَهُمْ كَيْفَ بَنَيْنَاهَا وَزَيَّنَّاهَا وَمَا لَهَا مِنْ فُرُوجٍ

129
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:19,460
Essentially, haven't they seen the perfection

130
00:06:19,460 --> 00:06:20,720
of the sky how it's been built,

131
00:06:20,720 --> 00:06:23,550
how it's been beautified, how it's got no blemishes in it.

132
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:28,904
وَالأَرْضَ مَدَدْنَاهَا وَأَلْقَيْنَا فِيهَا رَوَاسِيَ وَأَنْبَتْنَا فِيهَا مِنْ كُلِّ زَوْجٍ بَهِيجٍ

133
00:06:28,914 --> 00:06:32,640
The earth that's been stretched out, the
mountains that have been placed in it,

134
00:06:32,650 --> 00:06:35,910
the sprouting of all kinds of colorful pairs of

135
00:06:35,910 --> 00:06:38,350
fruits and vegetations that come out of the earth.

136
00:06:38,431 --> 00:06:40,800
تَبْصِرَةً
And all of that is so you can take a good look,

137
00:06:40,810 --> 00:06:42,511
وَذِكْرَى لِكُلِّ عَبْدٍ مُنِيبٍ

138
00:06:42,490 --> 00:06:44,850
and as a Reminder--how can it be a reminder?

139
00:06:45,030 --> 00:06:47,170
For a slave that is coming back to Allāh,

140
00:06:47,190 --> 00:06:49,510
whose heart is coming back to Allāh? How is it coming?

141
00:06:49,520 --> 00:06:51,449
How should it bring you back?

142
00:06:51,509 --> 00:06:55,959
وَنَزَّلْنَا مِنْ السَّمَاءِ مَاءً مُبَارَكًا فَأَنْبَتْنَا بِهِ جَنَّاتٍ وَحَبَّ الْحَصِيدِ

143
00:06:56,055 --> 00:07:00,999
وَالنَّخْلَ بَاسِقَاتٍ لَهَا طَلْعٌ نَضِيدٌ
رِزْقًا لِلْعِبَادِ

144
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:05,290
That We sent from the sky blessed water from the sky, by means

145
00:07:05,300 --> 00:07:10,110
of which gardens come out, crop comes out, palm trees that are outstretched,

146
00:07:10,110 --> 00:07:11,530
you know, uh,

147
00:07:11,540 --> 00:07:16,690
branches that extend. All of this is a provision for servants.

148
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:19,655
And then He says:
وَأَحْيَيْنَا بِهِ بَلْدَةً مَيْتًا

149
00:07:19,670 --> 00:07:20,605
And by means of that water

150
00:07:20,640 --> 00:07:23,030
We give a dead land life again.

151
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:27,127
And then He answers basically the first passage saying:
كَذَلِكَ الْخُرُوجُ

152
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:30,177
That's exactly how Resurrection is going to happen.

153
00:07:30,740 --> 00:07:32,500
Observe reality around you.

154
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:35,240
Observe these creations of the sky and the earth.

155
00:07:35,250 --> 00:07:38,150
And remind yourself that is how Resurrection will happen.

156
00:07:38,740 --> 00:07:40,630
But then Allāh addresses that

157
00:07:40,630 --> 00:07:43,220
maybe you-because they're so stubborn and so obnoxious

158
00:07:43,220 --> 00:07:45,360
they say, well, Allāh created a lot, He must be tired.

159
00:07:46,140 --> 00:07:47,460
So He's not going to create a second time.

160
00:07:48,540 --> 00:07:53,290
And so Allāh responds to that in the second last, which is just summarized in one āya,

161
00:07:53,550 --> 00:07:56,382
وَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالأَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا

162
00:07:57,262 --> 00:08:00,740
Doesn't that cover a summary of everything that I just explained to you?

163
00:08:00,750 --> 00:08:03,060
We created the skies, the earth, and whatever is between them.

164
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:05,600
And then He says, and the first time I did it:

165
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:08,324
فِي سِتَّةِ أَيَّامٍ وَمَا مَسَّنَا مِنْ لُغُوبٍ

166
00:08:08,350 --> 00:08:11,774
And We did it in six days and it did not hit Us with exhaustion.

167
00:08:11,990 --> 00:08:14,760
I'm not too tired to bring you back again.

168
00:08:15,740 --> 00:08:16,760
That will happen.

169
00:08:17,540 --> 00:08:20,170
The second passage, corresponding to the second last.

170
00:08:20,370 --> 00:08:22,360
You find then a switch in the sūra.

171
00:08:22,740 --> 00:08:27,050
كَذَّبَتْ قَبْلَهُمْ قَوْمُ نُوحٍ وَأَصْحَابُ الرَّسِّ وَثَمُودُ

172
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:29,890
وَعَادٌ وَفِرْعَوْنُ وَإِخْوَانُ لُوطٍ

173
00:08:29,870 --> 00:08:31,760
وَأَصْحَابُ الأَيْكَةِ وَقَوْمُ تُبَّعٍ

174
00:08:31,740 --> 00:08:33,609
What are these?

175
00:08:34,210 --> 00:08:37,870
Previously destroyed nations, all of whom denied messengers.

176
00:08:37,909 --> 00:08:40,679
People of Nụḥ, Aṣḥāb al-Rass,

177
00:08:40,679 --> 00:08:42,750
The People of Rass, Thamūd, 'Ād, Fir'awn,

178
00:08:42,750 --> 00:08:44,950
the Brethren of Lūṭ, the people of 'Īka,

179
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:46,720
the Nation of Tubba'. All of them.

180
00:08:46,730 --> 00:08:49,440
Allāh says, have I been exhausted by the creation the first time?

181
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:50,360
You're just confused.

182
00:08:50,360 --> 00:08:52,250
And I know what whispers come to you.

183
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:54,627
وَنَعْلَمُ مَا تُوَسْوِسُ بِهِ نَفْسُهُ

184
00:08:54,640 --> 00:08:58,467
We know what whispers hit the human being's inner self.

185
00:08:58,440 --> 00:09:00,960
But I'm closer to you than your vein, than your jugular vein.

186
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:03,160
When He says this all

187
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:06,750
it is contrasted directly in the third last passage.

188
00:09:06,750 --> 00:09:10,077
Allāh says:
وَكَمْ أَهْلَكْنَا قَبْلَهُمْ مِنْ قَرْنٍ

189
00:09:10,077 --> 00:09:12,260
How many nations in the past did We destroy?

190
00:09:12,850 --> 00:09:13,870
What is that echoing?

191
00:09:14,540 --> 00:09:16,760
All the nations that were listed that were destroyed.

192
00:09:17,210 --> 00:09:22,560
هُمْ أَشَدُّ مِنْهُمْ بَطْشًا فَنَقَّبُوا فِي الْبِلاَدِ هَلْ مِنْ مَحِيصٍ

193
00:09:22,620 --> 00:09:25,670
They were much more powerful than the Quraysh are.

194
00:09:25,670 --> 00:09:27,560
And they made much more of an imprint in the land.

195
00:09:27,570 --> 00:09:29,140
But do you find anything left of them?

196
00:09:29,150 --> 00:09:34,092
And then He says, I love this,
إِنَّ فِي ذَلِكَ لَذِكْرَى لِمَنْ كَانَ لَهُ قَلْبٌ

197
00:09:34,540 --> 00:09:38,050
There's a powerful reminder in all of this for anyone who possesses a heart.

198
00:09:39,140 --> 00:09:42,650
On the flip side, we were told there is a spiritual crisis inside us.

199
00:09:42,660 --> 00:09:45,150
There's waswasa happening inside the nafs.

200
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:47,740
Now we're told: yes, there is a nafs,

201
00:09:47,740 --> 00:09:50,610
there is an inner self, and there's constant whispers happening,

202
00:09:50,610 --> 00:09:52,230
pulling you into the wrong direction.

203
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:56,650
But you have also been empowered with a heart that is capable of reminder,

204
00:09:56,650 --> 00:10:00,180
that's very powerful that can pull you away from all of that waswasa.

205
00:10:00,190 --> 00:10:04,060
So the response to that waswasa is:
لِمَنْ كَانَ لَهُ قَلْبٌ

206
00:10:04,350 --> 00:10:08,873
And how will you enforce that heart?
وَ أَلْقَى السَّمْعَ وَهُوَ شَهِيدٌ

207
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:13,060
Who drops an ear, who listens carefully and as a result, what he witnesses changes.

208
00:10:13,740 --> 00:10:14,700
The view changes.

209
00:10:14,710 --> 00:10:17,840
You see the parallel between that section and this section,

210
00:10:17,850 --> 00:10:20,340
previous nations and then previous nations again.

211
00:10:20,350 --> 00:10:23,090
Then you come to the center of the sūra.

212
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:26,660
The center of the sūra is its own architecture. It's it's own design.

213
00:10:27,140 --> 00:10:29,870
So it's like the three at the top and the three at the bottom.

214
00:10:29,870 --> 00:10:33,780
I've given you like an A - B - C, and I've given you a C -B  and A.

215
00:10:33,790 --> 00:10:37,760
That's the outer rim of the sūra. Now we're inside the heart of the sūra.

216
00:10:38,140 --> 00:10:40,660
Inside the heart of the sūra, there are two passages.

217
00:10:41,340 --> 00:10:45,450
One passage takes you from death all the way to Judgment Day.

218
00:10:46,040 --> 00:10:47,440
That's one passage.

219
00:10:47,450 --> 00:10:53,130
The second passage takes you-- contrasts the life in Hell with the life in Heaven.

220
00:10:53,140 --> 00:10:58,270
So death to Judgment Day is one scene, and then Hell and Heaven is the second scene.

221
00:10:58,290 --> 00:11:01,170
So I'm going to describe a little bit of the first scene to you,

222
00:11:02,340 --> 00:11:04,330
and I'll walk you through its translation.

223
00:11:04,340 --> 00:11:06,407
Just elements of its translation.

224
00:11:06,407 --> 00:11:10,747
إِذْ يَتَلَقَّى الْمُتَلَقِّيَانِ عَنْ الْيَمِينِ وَعَنْ الشِّمَالِ قَعِيدٌ

225
00:11:10,777 --> 00:11:14,107
مَا يَلْفِظُ مِنْ قَوْلٍ إِلاَّ لَدَيْهِ رَقِيبٌ عَتِيدٌ

226
00:11:14,157 --> 00:11:20,627
When the two meet. The two that were on either side of you meet. And not a word has ever gone by--

227
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:23,990
you've never said a single word, except that it hasn't been watched over, recorded.

228
00:11:24,740 --> 00:11:25,990
All of it's been captured.

229
00:11:26,180 --> 00:11:30,308
وَجَاءَتْ سَكْرَةُ الْمَوْتِ بِالْحَقِّ ذَلِكَ مَا كُنْتَ مِنْهُ تَحِيدُ

230
00:11:30,370 --> 00:11:34,348
The pangs of death, the drunken state of death, finally hit.

231
00:11:34,540 --> 00:11:38,630
And this is the thing you've been avoiding all along. See, I told you these records,

232
00:11:38,640 --> 00:11:39,720
when are they meeting?

233
00:11:39,730 --> 00:11:43,290
When the person is about to, or when they're hitting death.

234
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:44,226
وَنُفِخَ فِي الصُّورِ

235
00:11:44,236 --> 00:11:47,910
And in the blink of an eye, the Horn is blown into.

236
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:51,590
The Horn is blown into. What is this talking about? The Day of Judgment.

237
00:11:51,743 --> 00:11:52,620
ذَلِكَ يَوْمُ الْوَعِيدِ

238
00:11:52,780 --> 00:11:54,660
That is the day that you were threatened with.

239
00:11:55,423 --> 00:11:58,066
وَجَاءَتْ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَعَهَا سَائِقٌ وَشَهِيدٌ

240
00:11:58,066 --> 00:11:59,930
And every person is going to have with them

241
00:11:59,930 --> 00:12:02,420
someone who pushes them forward, and a witness with them.

242
00:12:02,430 --> 00:12:05,322
Details. This is the
dars on Sūrat al-Qāf, listen to it.

243
00:12:05,430 --> 00:12:08,050
لَقَدْ كُنْتَ فِي غَفْلَةٍ مِنْ هَذَا

244
00:12:08,050 --> 00:12:10,720
You used to be completely oblivious about all of this.

245
00:12:10,730 --> 00:12:13,389
You had no clue any of this was coming.

246
00:12:13,389 --> 00:12:14,859
فَكَشَفْنَا عَنْكَ غِطَاءَكَ

247
00:12:14,840 --> 00:12:19,769
So We've removed your covers for you. We've uncovered the reality for you.

248
00:12:19,779 --> 00:12:21,639
فَبَصَرُكَ الْيَوْمَ حَدِيدٌ

249
00:12:21,649 --> 00:12:25,760
Your vision today is ironclad. It's-- you see crystal clear now.

250
00:12:26,340 --> 00:12:27,520
وَقَالَ قَرِينُهُ

251
00:12:27,530 --> 00:12:30,459
And the devil that accompanied him his whole life says:

252
00:12:30,469 --> 00:12:32,029
هَذَا مَا لَدَيَّ عَتِيدٌ

253
00:12:32,030 --> 00:12:34,300
This is the one I brought with me, this bad one.

254
00:12:34,329 --> 00:12:35,675
أَلْقِيَا فِي جَهَنَّمَ

255
00:12:35,655 --> 00:12:36,805
Throw in Hell

256
00:12:36,819 --> 00:12:37,815
كُلَّ كَفَّارٍ عَنِيدٍ

257
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:39,935
every ingrate, every stubborn one

258
00:12:39,935 --> 00:12:41,105
مَنَّاعٍ لِلْخَيْرِ

259
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:42,090
throw into Hell

260
00:12:42,070 --> 00:12:43,906
everyone that prevented good.

261
00:12:43,886 --> 00:12:44,826
مُعْتَدٍ مُرِيبٍ

262
00:12:44,840 --> 00:12:46,400
The one who was crossing the lines and

263
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:49,020
constantly making even others doubtful about the faith.

264
00:12:49,030 --> 00:12:50,780
الَّذِي جَعَلَ مَعَ اللَّهِ إِلَهًا آخَرَ

265
00:12:50,780 --> 00:12:54,189
Who put other gods besides Allāh, next to Allāh.

266
00:12:54,189 --> 00:12:55,849
فَأَلْقِيَاهُ فِي الْعَذَابِ الشَّدِيدِ

267
00:12:55,870 --> 00:12:57,820
Throw him into painful punishment.

268
00:12:57,830 --> 00:13:02,010
And this devil who says, 'Look at all this bad stuff he did, Ya Allāh throw him in Hell.'

269
00:13:02,020 --> 00:13:04,760
Then he says:
قَالَ قَرِينُهُ رَبَّنَا مَا أَطْغَيْتُهُ

270
00:13:05,240 --> 00:13:10,020
He says, 'By the way, Master, I didn't make him do it, okay?'

271
00:13:10,050 --> 00:13:12,370
وَلَكِنْ كَانَ فِي ضَلاَلٍ بَعِيدٍ

272
00:13:12,350 --> 00:13:14,310
'He was lost on his own.'

273
00:13:14,340 --> 00:13:19,880
I mean, this minion of Shayṭān has been working on getting you into Hell all this time.

274
00:13:19,890 --> 00:13:23,110
So when he comes before Allah, he says, 'I need to finish my mission,

275
00:13:23,130 --> 00:13:26,470
and it's gonna be, I got him to do a lot of stuff, but no, no, not me!'

276
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:27,560
'He did it.'

277
00:13:28,540 --> 00:13:31,107
Allah says:
قَالَ لاَ تَخْتَصِمُوا لَدَيَّ

278
00:13:31,197 --> 00:13:32,540
Don't argue before Me.

279
00:13:32,640 --> 00:13:34,189
وَقَدْ قَدَّمْتُ إِلَيْكُمْ بِالْوَعِيدِ

280
00:13:34,210 --> 00:13:38,160
And the Warning has come to all of you. Meaning you and your devil were all warned,

281
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:40,429
مَا يُبَدَّلُ الْقَوْلُ لَدَيَّ

282
00:13:40,459 --> 00:13:43,740
The word will not be changed in My presence.

283
00:13:43,740 --> 00:13:46,163
There is not going to be a different verdict now.

284
00:13:46,193 --> 00:13:47,765
وَمَا أَنَا بِظَلاَّمٍ لِلْعَبِيدِ

285
00:13:47,775 --> 00:13:49,550
And I'm not going to be oppressive to slaves.

286
00:13:50,040 --> 00:13:53,460
I'm not gonna do anybody wrong. Okay, this is passage--

287
00:13:53,470 --> 00:13:57,060
mini-passage one in the center of the sūra. I want you to go back.

288
00:13:58,240 --> 00:14:01,690
The first item we studied was "not a word will go unrecorded".

289
00:14:01,850 --> 00:14:02,650
Do you remember that?

290
00:14:03,830 --> 00:14:05,860
And it is "every word is being watched".

291
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:10,380
And the last āya of this passage says the word will not be changed.

292
00:14:10,380 --> 00:14:13,371
My word has come to pass. قول قول

293
00:14:13,371 --> 00:14:16,911
مَا يُبَدَّلُ الْقَوْلُ
مَا يَلْفِظُ مِنْ قَوْلٍ

294
00:14:17,040 --> 00:14:21,368
Okay? So where it starts is where it ends. Then Allah says,

295
00:14:21,368 --> 00:14:26,938
The drunken state of death came. This is what you were running away from.

296
00:14:27,450 --> 00:14:30,360
The Horn will be blown into.

297
00:14:30,910 --> 00:14:32,160
That's what you were warned about.

298
00:14:33,140 --> 00:14:36,560
You've been heedless about all of this because you were warned and you didn't care.

299
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:41,730
Now the the covers have been removed, and now you can see

300
00:14:41,950 --> 00:14:45,733
all of this was what? You ignored the warnings, you ignored the warnings,

301
00:14:45,790 --> 00:14:47,433
you ignored the warnings.

302
00:14:47,550 --> 00:14:50,710
And on the flip side, the second last--that was the second item--

303
00:14:50,710 --> 00:14:55,073
the second last item is don't argue in front of Me. The Warning already came.

304
00:14:55,750 --> 00:15:00,380
The Warning is in such detail. And by the second last side, the Warning has already came.

305
00:15:00,380 --> 00:15:03,340
And in the middle are the two statements of the qarīn.

306
00:15:03,350 --> 00:15:06,470
The qarīn, on the one hand, wants you to go to Hell, and on the other hand,

307
00:15:06,470 --> 00:15:07,650
doesn't want to go to Hell himself.

308
00:15:08,540 --> 00:15:11,060
So the reality of Shayṭān, who is gonna drop you on Judgment Day.

309
00:15:11,740 --> 00:15:12,250
Okay?

310
00:15:12,950 --> 00:15:17,270
That would be the symmetrical structure of part one of the middle of Sūrat Qāf.

311
00:15:17,640 --> 00:15:19,050
Then you come to part two.

312
00:15:20,350 --> 00:15:21,410
In part two.

313
00:15:21,510 --> 00:15:25,413
يَوْمَ نَقُولُ لِجَهَنَّمَ هَلْ امْتَلَأْتِ

314
00:15:25,443 --> 00:15:29,413
We say on that day to hell, 'Are you filled?' And it responds.

315
00:15:29,440 --> 00:15:30,240
هَلْ مِنْ مَزِيدٍ

316
00:15:30,340 --> 00:15:31,954
'Is there anymore?'

317
00:15:32,040 --> 00:15:36,500
And that one statement was enough to not have Allāh describe Hell any further.

318
00:15:37,740 --> 00:15:40,530
There is no further need for an explanation of

319
00:15:40,530 --> 00:15:42,700
the Fire, of the torture, of the punishment,

320
00:15:42,710 --> 00:15:46,470
because that statement is shocking and terrifying all on its own.

321
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:49,960
So the rest of this passage only deals with Jannah.

322
00:15:50,640 --> 00:15:53,760
وَأُزْلِفَتْ الْجَنَّةُ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ غَيْرَ بَعِيدٍ

323
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:59,040
Heaven will be brought close for people of taqwā; it's not far away.

324
00:15:59,060 --> 00:16:00,501
هَذَا مَا تُوعَدُونَ

325
00:16:00,551 --> 00:16:02,312
And (غير بعيد) is actually a play on words.

326
00:16:02,370 --> 00:16:05,613
It's actually from:
ذَلِكَ رَجْعٌ بَعِيدٌ

327
00:16:05,653 --> 00:16:08,032
And Allāh says for (متقين) don't worry, it's (متقين).

328
00:16:08,042 --> 00:16:10,998
هَذَا مَا تُوعَدُونَ لِكُلِّ أَوَّابٍ حَفِيظٍ

329
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:12,910
This is what you've been promised for everyone who

330
00:16:12,910 --> 00:16:15,490
keeps coming back to Allāh, safeguarding himself.

331
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:18,360
The one who was fearful of al-Raḥmān when he couldn't even see Him

332
00:16:18,370 --> 00:16:21,164
and came with a heart that keeps coming back.

333
00:16:21,184 --> 00:16:24,980
تَبْصِرَةً وَذِكْرَى لِكُلِّ عَبْدٍ مُنِيبٍ

334
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:27,400
And now,
وَجَاءَ بِقَلْبٍ مُنِيبٍ

335
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:30,470
ادْخُلُوهَا بِسَلاَمٍ
Enter safely

336
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:33,260
ذَلِكَ يَوْمُ الْخُلُودِ
That's the day of living forever.

337
00:16:33,340 --> 00:16:39,028
لَهُمْ مَا يَشَاءُونَ فِيهَا وَلَدَيْنَا مَزِيدٌ
They have whatever they want in it and We have even more in store for them.

338
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:42,480
So this brief passage, which contrasts simply Heaven and Hell.

339
00:16:42,490 --> 00:16:44,900
The interesting thing about it is the first of these āyāt said:

340
00:16:45,030 --> 00:16:48,600
وَتَقُولُ هَلْ مِنْ مَزِيدٍ
about Hell

341
00:16:48,600 --> 00:16:50,511
Hell says: is there anymore?

342
00:16:50,531 --> 00:16:53,260
And about Heaven, Allāh says they'll have everything they want and We've got more.

343
00:16:53,340 --> 00:16:56,970
The first āya ends with (مزيد); and the last of these āyāt also ends with (مزيد).

344
00:16:57,340 --> 00:16:59,510
So the verbal link is there, you know,

345
00:16:59,510 --> 00:17:01,890
creating a kind of symmetry between those two passages.

346
00:17:01,900 --> 00:17:06,760
So this is kind of an overall structure of Sūrat Qāf. Was that clear to everybody?

